---
/**
 * Price — Economics-lens concept at Interactive scale.
 * Relative signal of specialization and context advantage.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Price | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Economics lens · Interactive Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Price
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Relative signal of specialization and context advantage.
					Aggregates what others would allocate; legible under Relativity.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Core concept under the Economics lens.
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Not a requirement of fiat or platform token.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">What others would give up.</h2>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Price</strong> is the relative signal that emerges when Identities compare opportunity costs across a possible Exchange.
					It is not what one Identity wants. It is what the field of other Identities reveals they are willing to allocate for access, claim, context advantage, or outcome under their own scarcity and ownership.
				</p>
				<p>
					Under the Economics lens, Price sits on the Interactive scale next to Exchange.
					Opportunity is internal (what I forgo). Price is intersubjective (what others signal they would forgo).
					The two become comparable only when Exchange is possible.
				</p>
				<p>
					Price is graded and local. It can form between two Identities without a full Market.
					A stable Market is what makes many Prices coherent and discoverable at once.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Price is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Relative signal:</strong> aggregates willingness to allocate under others’ scarcity and preference.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Specialization marker:</strong> often tracks context advantage and comparative capability, not raw token count.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Bridge between Opportunity and Exchange:</strong> makes make-or-buy legible without dissolving ownership.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Legible under Relativity:</strong> observed from a position; no absolute global price without a shared frame.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Price is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not own Preference.</strong>
						Preference ranks my ends. Price reports what others would pay or allocate.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Mass.</strong>
						Mass remains emergent from interaction. Stating a price does not create geometric weight.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not mandatory platform currency.</strong>
						Price can be expressed in claims, grants, attention, or other agreed units.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the Exchange itself.</strong>
						Price is the signal; Exchange is the consented transfer under (or against) that signal.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Surface comparable signals</strong> when two Identities consider Exchange.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep Price attributable to observed willingness,</strong> not to declared prestige.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Compare external Price against own Opportunity</strong> before accepting or offering.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Avoid attention-auction dynamics</strong> that dissolve membrane consent.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
					<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Quick self-check</div>
					<ul class="space-y-3 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						<li>What is the external Price for this access or outcome relative to my Opportunity?</li>
						<li>Whose willingness does this signal actually reflect?</li>
						<li>Would accepting this Price strengthen or erode Stem coherence?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Related</div>
					<p>
						Prior: Opportunity (Single) → <a href="/framework/exchange" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Exchange</a>.
						Next scale: <a href="/framework/market" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Market</a> (Collective).
						Physics parallel: Relativity and Gravitation.
						Biology parallel: recognition signals that gate coupling.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/exchange" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Exchange</a>
					<a href="/framework/market" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Market</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
